  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal Protection Study Beira</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Coastal Protection Project (CPP) entails the preparation of a feasibility study including a preliminary design for the selected preferred coastal protection scheme for Beira. It aims to develop a strategy to protect Beira and its over 600,000 citizens against sea hazards, flooding, and other climate-related disasters. It also includes an Environmental Pre-Feasibility Study and Scoping Definition (EPDA) and the development of an Implementation Strategy for the next phases.
The CPP consortium is led by Royal HaskoningDHV (based in the Netherlands and Mozambique), with partners Deltares (the Netherlands), Witteveen+Bos (the Netherlands) and Metier (Mozambique). NLRC, will acst as independent observer to ensure that the needs of local communities form the core of the coastal protection plan for Beira.</narrative>
  </description>
